#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Menu Items/Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction to the Menubar and Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The key to getting the most out of &kword;, is found in the menu bars and "
"the toolbars."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The menubar is organized into groups of functions (&eg; file functions, "
"table functions, &etc;). Below each of these groups, is a submenu of "
"actions. Some of these submenus will have sub menus of their own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The toolbars are also organized into groups. Each toolbar consists of a set "
"of buttons. Each button performs a specific function. The toolbars are "
"designed to act as shortcuts for more commonly used functions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first part of this section of the manual discusses the manipulation of "
"&kword;'s toolbars to suit your needs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The second part of this section, takes a detailed look at each menubar "
"function, and each standard toolbar button, and provides you with a brief "
"summary of its action. Many of these sections also provide you with a link "
"to more detailed information located elsewhere in the &kword; Handbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hiding, Changing, and Moving Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: mbtb.docbook:47 mbtb.docbook:69 mbtb.docbook:130 mbtb.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mbtb.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "hiding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; offers the user great flexibility when it comes to toolbars. This "
"first section will show you some of the many options you have for "
"relocating, reformatting and removing toolbars."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hiding Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &kword; for the first time, several toolbars are visible. If "
"you don't think you will need a toolbar, and want to reclaim that desktop "
"space, you can hide any or all of the toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To hide a toolbar, Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Toolbars</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. "
"This will bring up a submenu. All of the toolbars are listed. Simply select "
"the toolbar you want to hide or restore."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Moving Toolbars around"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mbtb.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "moving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbars can be located on the screen in 5 places."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Top</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr "Inferior"

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left"
msgstr "Esquèrra"

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right"
msgstr "Drecha"

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Floating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Top</guilabel>, <guilabel>Bottom</guilabel>, <guilabel>Left</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Right</guilabel> refer to the edges of the &kword; "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By locating a toolbar in the <guilabel>Bottom</guilabel> position, for "
"example, you move the toolbar into a horizontal position below the Document "
"Area, and along the bottom of the &kword; window. By locating a toolbar in "
"the <guilabel>Left</guilabel> position,however, you move the toolbar into a "
"vertical position to the left of the Document Area, and along the left edge "
"of the &kword; window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multiple toolbars can be located at each of these points in the screen. (You "
"could, for instance, move all the toolbars to the top of the screen). "
"&kword; will shuffle toolbars around, to fit in the most compact way at that "
"location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to move any toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the striped area of the toolbar with the &LMB; and hold the button "
"down. Drag the toolbar to the desired location. You will see a rectangular "
"shape indicating the position and orientation of the toolbar. When at the "
"desired location, release the &LMB; and the toolbar will be inserted there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>or</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the toolbar with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. Select "
"<guimenuitem>Orientation</guimenuitem>. A small submenu will appear. Select "
"<guimenuitem>Top</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Bottom</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Left</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Right</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Floating</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Flat</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select <guilabel>Floating</guilabel> for any toolbar, a new window "
"will be created just for that toolbar. This window can be moved "
"independently from the &kword; window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, if you select <guilabel>Flat</guilabel> for any toolbar, the "
"toolbar will be reduced to a horizontal section of lines located directly "
"below the menubar. To restore this menubar, simply double click with the "
"&LMB; on the flattened toolbar and the toolbar will be restored to its "
"original size and position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the look of your toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mbtb.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toolbars can have their buttons displayed different ways. Below are examples "
"of the four options for the <emphasis>File</emphasis> toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: mbtb.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icons Only"
msgstr "Sonque icònas"

#. Tag: entry
#: mbtb.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Only"
msgstr "Sonque tèxt"

#. Tag: entry
#: mbtb.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Aside Icons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: mbtb.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Under Icons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the appearance of a toolbar, place the cursor over on the toolbar "
"you want to change, and click with the &RMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A small menu will appear at the mouse cursor. Select <guimenuitem>Text "
"Position</guimenuitem>. This will open a submenu, select your preference "
"from the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing Icon Size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: mbtb.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "changing size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also select the size of the icons by clicking on the toolbar with "
"the &RMB;. A small popup menu will appear. Select <guimenuitem>Icon Size</"
"guimenuitem> and then your preferred icon size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting the look of one toolbar does not alter the look of another toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menubar"
msgstr "Barra de menuts"

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Menubar contains all commands available to &kword;. It is divided into "
"10 general categories."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking on the <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu, you can begin new "
"documents, load previously edited documents, print your documents, close the "
"current document (so you can load another document), or quit &kword; "
"entirely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action> Allows you to open new files for editing.</action> For Step by Step "
"instructions see <link linkend=\"new-doc\">Beginning a New Document</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"filenew2.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action> For opening previously created</action> &kword; files. For Step by "
"Step instructions see <link linkend=\"loading\">Retrieving a Saved Document</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"fileopen.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to "
"using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guisubmenu>Open Recent</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For opening the most recently edited files. Once you have clicked on this "
"option, a list of recently edited files will appear. Select the file you "
"want and &kword; will open the file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Saves your current file to disk.</action> If you have not saved the "
"file yet, you will be prompted for a filename. For more details, see <link "
"linkend=\"saving\">Saving a Document</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"filefloppy.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to "
"using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to save your file under another name or another format.</"
"action> For more details, see <link linkend=\"command-save-as\">Saving a "
"Document</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Reload</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reloads the current file from disk, erasing any changes to the document "
"since the last time it was saved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Will load a file from another application.</action> &kword; attempts "
"to decipher as much of the file as it can. For many files, some information "
"will be lost. For more information on the ability to import files from other "
"applications, see the section on <link linkend=\"filters\">filters</link> at "
"the end of this documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Will save a file using the format of another application.</action> "
"&kword; attempts to save as much of the file as it can. For many files, some "
"information will be lost. For more information on the ability to export "
"files to other applications, see the section on <link linkend=\"filters"
"\">filters</link> at the end of this documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Mail...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Launches your email client so you can send the current file as an "
"attachment. The file must have been saved once before this option can be "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Create Template From Document...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to save your file as a template, to use as a starting "
"point for future documents.</action> For more details, see <link linkend="
"\"template-creation\">Creating a new template</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Statistics</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a window that counts the sentences, words, characters and syllables in "
"your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number of sentences is not always absolutely correct, as &kword; has to "
"guess if a dot really starts a new sentence or not. The number of syllables "
"is estimated, &kword; therefore assumes that the text is written in English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Flesch reading ease:</guilabel> score is a number between 0 "
"and 100 which estimates how readable a text is. The higher the number, the "
"easier the text can be read. Text with a score of 70-80 should have fairly "
"good readability."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:384
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Flesch formula uses the number of words per sentences and the number of "
"syllables per word. It assumes that the use of short words and short "
"sentences increases the readability of a text. It says nothing about grammar "
"or meaning. As both the number of sentences and the number of syllables is "
"estimated, the result is not absolutely precise. The text should be at least "
"200 words long, if it isn't the score will be marked as approximated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Flesch score is defined for English text only, but the basic idea should "
"work for many other languages, too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to dismiss the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Print the file.</action> For an overview of printing options see "
"<link linkend=\"printing\">Printing a Document</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"fileprint.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> are equivalent to "
"using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print Preview...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Print the file, but sends the output to your postscript viewer, for your "
"confirmation before sending it to the printer. The operation of your "
"postscript viewer will vary depending on which viewer you use. Refer to the "
"help files for your viewer for help."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"fileprint2.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:440
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Document Information</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Opens a window that lets you enter information related to the "
"document</action> (such as author's name, address, phone numbers, document "
"abstract, &etc;). This information is saved with the document for later "
"classification."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information, see <link linkend=\"documentinfo\">Document "
"Information</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>W</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Close</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the file you are currently working on. If you have not saved your most "
"recent changes, you will be prompted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>W</keycap></keycombo> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:479
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Quits</action> &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:489
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By clicking on the <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> menu, you can cut/copy/paste "
"text, undo or redo edits and perform searches and text replacement."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Reverses the last action you performed.</action> Not all actions can "
"be reversed. If you are not able to Undo the last action, the "
"<guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem> option will be displayed gray and is not "
"accessible. For a more thourough discussion of Undo/Redo, <link linkend="
"\"undo-redo\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"undo.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>&Shift;</"
"keycap><keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Redo</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Reverses the last Undo performed.</action> If the Redo option is "
"unavailable, the Toolbar will display this items gray. For a more thourough "
"discussion of Undo/Redo, <link linkend=\"undo-redo\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>&Shift;</keycap><keycap>Z</"
"keycap></keycombo> or clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"redo.png\" format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>X</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Deletes the highlighted text from the document, and places a copy in "
"the clipboard.</action> For a more complete directions on cutting and "
"pasting, and a full description of the clipboard, <link linkend=\"clipboard"
"\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>X</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"editcut.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Places a copy of the highlighted text in the clipboard, without "
"changing the text in the document.</action> For a more complete directions "
"on cutting and pasting, and a full description of the clipboard, <link "
"linkend=\"clipboard\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"editcopy.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Inserts a copy of the clipboard into the current cursor position.</"
"action> If there is highlighted text, &kword; replaces replaces all "
"highlighted text with the contents of the clipboard. The clipboard is not "
"altered. For a more complete directions on cutting and pasting, and a full "
"description of the clipboard, <link linkend=\"clipboard\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"editpaste.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Select All</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "Immediately highlights all text of the current frameset."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Select All Frames</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid "Immediately selects all frames in the current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Select Frame</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects the current text frame in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to search for a series of characters.</action> The find "
"features of &kword; are covered in more detail under <link linkend=\"search-"
"and-replace\">Searching for Text</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"find.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Next</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Repeat the last search for characters starting at the current cursor "
"position.</action> The find features of &kword; are covered in more detail "
"under <link linkend=\"search-and-replace\">Searching for Text</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Previous</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Repeat the last search for characters starting at the current cursor "
"position and moving backwards.</action> The find features of &kword; are "
"covered in more detail under <link linkend=\"search-and-replace\">Searching "
"for Text</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Replace...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:719
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to replace one or more characters with another set of "
"characters.</action> The find and replace features of &kword; are covered in "
"more detail under <link linkend=\"replace\">Replacing Text</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> is "
"equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Delete Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete the current page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:745
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>New View</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:750
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will create a new view of your document.</action> For more "
"information on views, refer to the section entitled <link linkend=\"views"
"\">Using Multiple Views</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:758
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>W</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Close All Views</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will close all views including the current view. This will also "
"quit &kword;.</action> For more information on views, refer to the section "
"entitled <link linkend=\"views\">Using Multiple Views</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Split View</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:779
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will split the current view.</action> The orientation of the "
"split is determined by the <guimenuitem>Splitter Orientation</guimenuitem>. "
"For more information on views, refer to the section entitled <link linkend="
"\"views\">Using Multiple Views</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:789
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Remove View</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will close the current view.</action> For more information on "
"views, refer to the section entitled <link linkend=\"views\">Using Multiple "
"Views</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Splitter Orientation</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:807
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This determines whether split views are oriented horizontally or "
"vertically.</action> Click on this option, and you are presented with a "
"submenu with 2 options: <guimenuitem>Vertical</guimenuitem> and "
"<guimenuitem>Horizontal</guimenuitem>. For more information on views, refer "
"to the section entitled <link linkend=\"views\">Using Multiple Views</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:819
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Display Mode</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:824
#, no-c-format
msgid "When this option is selected, a submenu opens with 3 options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: mbtb.docbook:826
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Page Mode</guilabel> - &kword; will show you how your page looks "
"in a WYSIWYG environment. This is the standard view for editing your "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: mbtb.docbook:828
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Preview Mode</guilabel> - This changes &kword; from a single page "
"view, to a multiple page view suitable for evaluating document flow and "
"formatting. The number of pages shown in preview mode <link linkend=\"opt-ui"
"\">can be adjusted</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: mbtb.docbook:830
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Text Mode</guilabel> - When this option is selected, &kword; will "
"only show the text of your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:836
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Formatting Characters</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:841
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on this option toggles the display of formatting characters. "
"Selecting this option will display non-printable characters (spaces, "
"character returns, and tab stops). Selecting this option again will turn the "
"display of these characters off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:845
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Which formatting characters are visible can be configured in the <link "
"linkend=\"opt-misc\">&kword; configuration dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:852
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Borders</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:857
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on this option toggles the display of the borders to frames. "
"Normally, &kword; draws a gray line around each frame, so you can see the "
"borders of the frames. If you want this option turned off, you can select "
"this option. Selecting this option again will turn the borders back on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:867
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show/Hide Doc Structure</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:872
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Clicking on this option toggles the display of the document "
"structure window.</action> For more information, refer to the section "
"entitled <link linkend=\"doc-structure\">Document Structure</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:880
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show/Hide Rulers</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:885
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will toggle the rulers off.</action> Selecting "
"this option again will turn rulers on. More information on rulers can be "
"found under <link linkend=\"rulers\">Using rulers</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show/Hide Grid</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:899
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will toggle the grid on.</action> Selecting "
"this option again will turn grid off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:906
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Snap to Grid</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:911
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will toggle the snap to grid on.</action> "
"Selecting this option again will turn snap to grid off. A checkmark before "
"the menu entry will show you the current status of this option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:920
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Zoom</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting this option will let you increase or decrease the page "
"magnification. Selecting a zoom value larger than 100 percent causes the "
"text and pictures to appear larger. Selecting a zoom value smaller than 100 "
"percent will cause the text and pictures to appear smaller."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:932
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The zoom value does not affect the final output of the text or pictures. "
"This option is intended to help you edit and layout your documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:942
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt; &Shift; <keycap>C</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Special "
"Character...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a dialog box which allows you to select characters not found on the "
"keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:956
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt; &Shift; <keycap>C</keycap></"
"keycombo> is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Return</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page Break</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will enter a special character which will force text into the "
"next connected text frame (Page Layout Templates) or the next page (Text "
"Oriented Templates).</action> More information can be found at <link linkend="
"\"hard-break\">Page Breaks</link> located in the <link linkend=\"frames"
"\">Working with Frames</link> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:976
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Return</keycap></keycombo> "
"is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:984
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:989
#, no-c-format
msgid "This option will insert a new page at the current cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:994
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Footnote/Endnote...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:999
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will insert a footnote or endnote at the current cursor "
"position.</action> More detailed information can be found in <link linkend="
"\"endnotes-and-footnotes\">Footnotes and Endnotes</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table of Contents</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1012
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will insert or update a table of contents at the current cursor "
"position.</action> More detailed information can be found in <link linkend="
"\"toc\">Table of Contents</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1020
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guisubmenu>Variable</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1025
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will allow you to insert page numbers, date, "
"time, author information, &etc;</action> You can find specific information "
"about page numbers <link linkend=\"page-number\">here</link>. More "
"information about Date and Times can be found under <link linkend=\"date-time"
"\">Inserting the Date and Time</link>. More information on other variables "
"can be found in <link linkend=\"variables\">Document Variables</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1037
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guisubmenu>Expression</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1042
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will allow you to insert common phrases.</"
"action> The phrases are organized into categories. For information on using "
"and adding expressions refer to the section entitled <link linkend="
"\"expressions\">Expressions</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1051
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Link...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1056
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to connect text to an external web page, email address or "
"files</action> For more information refer to the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"links\">Document Links</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1065
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Comment...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1070
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to add comments to selected text.</action> For more "
"information refer to the section entitled <link linkend=\"comments"
"\">Document Comments</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1078
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>File...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1083
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to insert another &kword; file within the document.</"
"action> For more information refer to the section entitled <link linkend="
"\"insert-file\">Inserting Files</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1091
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Bookmark...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1096
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to mark your place in the document for easy retrieval.</"
"action> For more information refer to the section entitled <link linkend="
"\"bookmarks\">Document Bookmarks</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will allow you to create a table in the current cursor location."
"</action> For more information, please see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"tables\">Tables</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> or clicking "
"<inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"part-kspread.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> are equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Picture...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action> This option will let you create a new frame, and automatically "
"insert a picture from a file into the new frame.</action> After selecting "
"this menu item or toolbar button, a dialog box will be opened, so you may "
"select the picture file from your system. (For help with this dialog box, "
"please see <link linkend=\"insert-graphics\">Inserting Graphics</link>.) "
"Once you have selected the file you want, click on the <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton> button. &kword; will close the dialog box, and your cursor will "
"change to cross hairs. Locate the cursor on the page where you would like to "
"locate one corner of your picture. Click and hold the &LMB;, then drag the "
"mouse. This will create a border which represents the final size of the "
"picture in your document. When you are happy with the size of the picture, "
"release the mouse button and the picture will be inserted in your new frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"fpicture.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F10</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Text Frame</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>To create a new text frame.</action> After selecting this option, "
"your cursor will change to cross hairs. Choose the location of one corner of "
"your new text frame. Click on the &LMB; and hold the button down. Drag the "
"mouse, until you have the desired text frame. When you have the correct "
"shape and size, release the mouse button. &kword; will now bring up a dialog "
"box with options to connect this text frame to other frames in your "
"document. For more information on this subject, see <link linkend=\"frames"
"\">Working with Frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F10</keycap></keycombo> or "
"clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"tfcreatebut.png"
"\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F4</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Formula</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Insert a formula into the document.</action> More information on "
"formulas in &kword; can be found <link linkend=\"formulas\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F4</keycap></keycombo> or clicking "
"<inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"part-kformula.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> are equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1207
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guisubmenu>Object Frame</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Creates a new frame, and opens a dialog box listing each of the &koffice; "
"applications. This will allow you to insert any data into your &kword; "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"kpart.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1223
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Scan Image...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to access your scanner for inserting pictures into your "
"document.</action> For more information see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"scan-graphics\">Using a picture from a scanner</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:1237
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1241
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Default Format</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automatically changes all formating back to the default settings for the "
"selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default format can be set with the <link linkend=\"opt-document"
"\">Document Configuration</link> options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Font...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action> Allows you to change the formatting characteristics of the selected "
"text.</action> For more details, go to <link linkend=\"format-characters"
"\">Formating Characters</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> "
"is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1285
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>To change the indenting, spacing between paragraphs, text flow, tab "
"stops, numbering and borders.</action> For more details, go to <link linkend="
"\"format-para\">Formating Paragraphs</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo> "
"is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1296
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Footnote...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to change the look of your footnotes.</action> For more "
"information see <link linkend=\"endnotes-and-footnotes\"> Footnotes</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1309
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guisubmenu>Formula</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to format the selected formula.</action> For more "
"information go to <link linkend=\"formulas\">Formulas</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1321
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guisubmenu>Style</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to select a style for the selected text. Selecting this option "
"shows a submenu listing all available paragraphs styles. Select the correct "
"style and the paragraph style will be changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1328
#, no-c-format
msgid "For more information go to <link linkend=\"styles\">Text Styles</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Style Manager..."
"</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Opens a dialog to allow you to format, add and delete styles.</"
"action> For more information go to <link linkend=\"styles\">Styles</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo> "
"is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1353
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import Styles...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1358
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to import a style.</action> For more information go to "
"<link linkend=\"styles\">Text Styles</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Create Style From Selection...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1370
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uses the currently selected text to create a new style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information go to <link linkend=\"style-add-text\">Text Styles</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1378
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page Layout...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Use this to alter the properties of the printed page, including "
"size, headers and footers.</action> For more details, go to <link linkend="
"\"page-format\">Formating the Page</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable/Disable Document Headers</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will toggle headers on.</action> Selecting "
"this option again will turn headers off. More information on headers and "
"footers can be found under <link linkend=\"headers-and-footers\">Headers and "
"Footers</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Enable/Disable Document Footers</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Selecting this option will toggle footers on.</action> Selecting "
"this option again will turn footers off. More information on headers and "
"footers can be found under <link linkend=\"headers-and-footers\">Headers and "
"Footers</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:1424
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame/Frameset Properties...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to configure basic formating options for the frameset.</"
"action> More information on this subject can be found in <link linkend="
"\"format-frame\">Setting properties for frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1443
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Delete Frame</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will allow you to delete the entire frame, and all of the text and "
"objects contained within the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1455
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>R</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Raise Frame</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1463
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will allow you to raise the frame up one level.</action> For "
"more information see the section entitled <link linkend=\"raise-frame"
"\">Raise and Lower frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> "
"is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>L</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Lower Frame</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will allow you to lower the frame down one level.</action> For "
"more information see the section entitled <link linkend=\"raise-frame"
"\">Raise and Lower frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>L</keycap></keycombo> "
"is equivalent to using the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1489
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Bring to Front</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This raises the currently selected frame to the top of all "
"overlapping frames.</action> For more information see the section entitled "
"<link linkend=\"raise-frame\">Raise and Lower frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1501
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Send to Back</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This lowers the currently selected frame to the bottom of all "
"overlapping frames.</action> For more information see the section entitled "
"<link linkend=\"raise-frame\">Raise and Lower frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1513
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Create Linked Copy</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Creates a duplicate frame. The contents of the new frame will automatically "
"be updated to match the contents of the old frame. As you continue to edit "
"the document, changes to one of these frames will result in the same changes "
"to the other frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1524
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Convert to Text Box</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selected text is removed from the current frame. A new frame is created to "
"allow the selected text to be inserted, and the new text frame is inserted "
"into the current document. This is an easy way to remove a section of text "
"and place it in a text box of its own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1535
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Style Manager...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to edit the frame styles.</action> For more information "
"see the section entitled <link linkend=\"framestyles\">Using frame styles</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Create Framestyle From Frame...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Create a new framestyle based on the currently selected frame.</"
"action> For more information see the section entitled <link linkend="
"\"framestyles\">Using Framestyles</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1559
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guisubmenu>Framestyle</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1564
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to format the selected frame(s) with a predefined "
"framestyle.</action> For more information see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"framestyles\">Using frame styles</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1571
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Frame Background Color...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1576
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will allow you to change the background color of the current frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1582
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure Frame Border</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: mbtb.docbook:1587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will allow you to change the border surrounding the current frame. When "
"selected, a submenu will appear with all available border styles. Select the "
"correct style and the borders are instantly changed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:1601
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1607
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1612
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to change the number of rows and columns in a table.</"
"action> For more on tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Row</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Insert "
"Row...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to insert a row into a table.</action> For more on "
"tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1626
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"rowin.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1634
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Row</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Delete "
"Selected Rows...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Delete a row from a table.</action> For more on tables, <link "
"linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"rowout.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Insert "
"Column...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1655
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to insert a column into a table.</action> For more on "
"tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1657
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"colin.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1665
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Delete "
"Selected Columns...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1670
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Delete a column from a table.</action> For more on tables, <link "
"linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"colout.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> is equivalent to using "
"the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1680
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Column</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Resize "
"Column...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Change the width of the currently selected column.</action> For more "
"on changing column widths, <link linkend=\"table-resize-column\">click here</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1692
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Cell</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Join "
"Cells</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1697
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will convert two (or more) separate cells into a single cell.</"
"action> For more on tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1705
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Cell</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Split "
"Cell...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1710
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This will split one cell into multiple smaller cells.</action> For "
"more on tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1717
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Cell</guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Protect "
"Cells</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1722
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This prevent changes to the data in the selected cells.</action> For "
"more on tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1729
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Ungroup Table</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1734
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Converts a table into a grid of individual frames.</action> These "
"individual frames are not connected and can be moved independently around "
"the page. For more on tables, <link linkend=\"tables\">click here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1741
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Delete Table</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Deletes the table the cursor is in.</action> You can find more about "
"tables in the section entitled <link linkend=\"tables\">Tables</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1753
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Table Style Manager...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1758
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Lets you edit tablestyles.</action> You can find more about tables "
"in the section entitled <link linkend=\"tablestyle\">Using Tablestyle</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1765
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guisubmenu>Tablestyle</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1770
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Lets you format the currently selected table using a preformatted "
"template.</action> You can find more about tables in the section entitled "
"<link linkend=\"tablestyle\">Using Tablestyle</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: mbtb.docbook:1777
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Table</guimenu><guimenuitem>Convert Table to Text</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:1782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Converts data that is currently in the selected table to regular "
