#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:2392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting Colors from a <guilabel>Select Color</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: mbtb.docbook:2393
#, no-c-format
msgid "selecting a color"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; uses a common dialog box any time the user needs to select a color "
"for an object (text, backgrounds, borders, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2396
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section will go into some detail on how to use this color dialog to "
"choose the best color for your object."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2397
#, no-c-format
msgid "When it is necessary to select a color, a dialog box appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The color dialog is an incredibly flexible dialog box, which makes it "
"possible to select colors in one of six different methods:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: mbtb.docbook:2407
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spectrum selectors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spectrum selectors consists of a square to adjust <glossterm linkend="
"\"defhue\">Hue</glossterm> and <glossterm linkend=\"defsaturation"
"\">Saturation</glossterm>, and a tall narrow box to adjust <glossterm "
"linkend=\"defvalue\">Value</glossterm>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The white cross hairs in the box show the currently selected color on the "
"spectrum. Drag the cross hairs up to increase <glossterm linkend="
"\"defsaturation\">saturation</glossterm>. Drag down to decrease <glossterm "
"linkend=\"defsaturation\">saturation</glossterm>. Move the cross hairs left "
"or right to change the <glossterm linkend=\"defhue\">hue</glossterm>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To adjust the <glossterm linkend=\"defvalue\">value</glossterm> of the "
"color, use the tall, narrow box to move the black arrow. Sliding the arrow "
"up increases the color's <glossterm linkend=\"defvalue\">value</glossterm>. "
"Sliding the arrow down decreases the color's <glossterm linkend=\"defvalue"
"\">value</glossterm>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2416 mbtb.docbook:2424 mbtb.docbook:2431 mbtb.docbook:2454
#: mbtb.docbook:2463 mbtb.docbook:2471
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The currently selected color is visible in the colored square below the "
"<guibutton>Add to Custom Colors</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: mbtb.docbook:2419
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hue, Saturation and Value"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the three spin boxes labeled <guilabel>H</guilabel>,<guilabel>S</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>V</guilabel>, a user can specify the <glossterm "
"linkend=\"defhue\">Hue</glossterm> (Range 0-359), <glossterm linkend="
"\"defsaturation\">Saturation</glossterm> (Range 0-255) and <glossterm "
"linkend=\"defvalue\">Value</glossterm> (Range 0-255) respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: mbtb.docbook:2428
#, no-c-format
msgid "Red, Green and Blue"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the three spin boxes labeled <guilabel>R</guilabel>,<guilabel>G</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>B</guilabel>, a user can specify the amount of Red, "
"Green and Blue to be mixed to form the current color. All three boxes can be "
"set to any value from 0-255."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: mbtb.docbook:2435
#, no-c-format
msgid "Palettes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A palette is a group of related colors. These colors are all made available "
"for easy selection according to a meaningful association."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select a new palette, click on the combo box at the top of the palette "
"selection area. You will be presented with several choices:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2440
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Recent Colors</guilabel> - This is a list of the most recently "
"used colors in your document. You can use this palette to maintain "
"consistency. As each new color is selected, it is automatically added to the "
"recent colors palette."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Custom Colors</guilabel> - You can create your own custom palette. "
"This is done by selecting a color using one of the other color selection "
"options, and clicking on <guibutton>Add to Custom Colors</guibutton>. That "
"color is now added to your custom color palette."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Forty Colors</guilabel> - This is a list of 40 commonly used "
"colors. This is a good palette to choose from if some of the people viewing "
"your document will be on machines with limited color capability."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Web Colors</guilabel> - This is a predefined palette of colors "
"that you might find useful for designing web pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Royal Colors</guilabel> - This is a predefined palette of colors "
"including numerous shades of purple and yellow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Named Colors</guilabel> - This is a list of color names. The names "
"are based on standard X server color names. The names are designed to give "
"descriptive names to each color. Simply select the name you want."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected a palette, you will be presented with a small square "
"showing each color available in the palette. To select a color from the "
"palette, simply click on the square of the desired color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: mbtb.docbook:2458
#, no-c-format
msgid "Eye dropper"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2459
#, no-c-format
msgid "The eye dropper can be used to sample a color from the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the eye dropper button is clicked, the cursor becomes crosshairs. "
"Simply place the crosshairs over any spot on the screen and click once. "
"&kword; will detect the selected color and automatically change the current "
"color to match the selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2462
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is especially useful for matching color elements between previously "
"created elements and new items."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: mbtb.docbook:2466
#, no-c-format
msgid "HTML code"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2467
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you know the HTML color code you want to use, you can enter it into the "
"text box labeled <guilabel>HTML:</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2469
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on HTML color codes, visit the <ulink url=\"http://"
"hotwired.lycos.com/webmonkey/reference/color_codes/\">Web monkey</ulink> "
"color code page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the color is selected, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to make that the "
"current color for your text, border, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2476
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to abort the color selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: mbtb.docbook:2479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting files using the file dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: mbtb.docbook:2480
#, no-c-format
msgid "using file dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; uses a common dialog box for all file related actions (saving, "
"loading, or selecting new files for insertion into the document). An example "
"is shown below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section will look more closely at this dialog and provided detailed "
"information on its use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2492
#, no-c-format
msgid "We will begin at the top of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: mbtb.docbook:2494
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbar"
msgstr "Barra d'espleches"

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2496
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The current location on the drive is listed at the top-center of the dialog. "
"This example dialog shows the current folder is <filename class=\"directory"
"\">/home/mmcbride/kword</filename>. If you click on this drop down box, you "
"will see common and recently visited folders. By selecting one of these "
"folders, you will be immediately moved to that folder and the dialog box "
"will update the file list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the upper left corner, is a blue arrow pointed up. This arrow will take "
"you up one level in the folder structure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next two buttons are back and forward buttons. These buttons work just "
"like those in an Internet browser. You can use the <guiicon>Back</guiicon> "
"button to travel to the previous folder, and the <guiicon>Forward</guiicon> "
"button to advance into a folder you just came from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2510
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next to the arrow buttons, is a <guiicon>Reload</guiicon> button. Clicking "
"this button, causes &kword; to reload the current folder if new files have "
"been added or deleted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2514
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To the right of the <guiicon>Reload</guiicon> button, is a blue file folder "
"with a starburst. This button will let you create a new folder and name it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2517
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next to the new folder button, is a button with a star on it. This button "
"allows you to set and navigate through bookmarks. This is a quick way to "
"jump to commonly accessed folders. By clicking this button, a submenu "
"appears which allows you to add bookmarks or jump to a new bookmark."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next to the bookmark button, is a button with a wrench on it. Clicking this "
"button brings up a sub menu with several entries:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2528
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sorting"
msgstr "A s'ordenar"

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2530
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, a submenu will appear allowing you to sort your "
"files by name, date or size. You can sort them forward or reversed. You can "
"also determine if folders should be listed before files, or mixed within the "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2536
#, no-c-format
msgid "Short View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, only the names of the files and folders will be "
"shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2539
#, no-c-format
msgid "Compare this to detailed view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2544
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detailed View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the names, sizes, dates, permisions, file owners "
"and group ownerships are shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2547
#, no-c-format
msgid "Compare this to short view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2552
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show Hidden Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will toggle between revealing and hiding normally hidden files. In most "
"cases you will want to leave this option off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2559
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show/Hide Quick Access Navigation Panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tall box along the left side of the dialog with a dark grey backround is "
"the Quick Navigation Panel. You can use this option to toggle whether it is "
"visible or not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"More detailed information about hte Quick Navigation Panel is avialable "
"further down this page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2567
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show/Hide Preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this option to toggle whether the preview panel is visible or "
"not. Typically, the preview panel is left off, but it can be useful when "
"looking for a picture to insert into a document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: mbtb.docbook:2574
#, no-c-format
msgid "Separate Folders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2576
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this option to toggle between a 2 pane view of the filesystem and a one "
"pane view of the filesystem. Most people will not need to worry about this "
"option as most people prefer the one pane view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: mbtb.docbook:2583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Navigation Bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2585
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Along the left side of the dialog box, is a column that contains several "
"icons. You can think of each of these icons as a shortcut to another "
"subfolder. If you click on an icon, you will be immediately moved to that "
"location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can add/edit or delete entries from the Location Bar. Simply click with "
"the &RMB; and a small popup menu will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: mbtb.docbook:2593
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Name and Filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text box labeled <guilabel>Location:</guilabel> contains the current "
"filename <filename>Resume.kwd</filename>. This text box will contain the "
"filename of the currently selected file when loading new documents or files "
"into &kword;. When saving a file, you will enter the desired filename in "
"this text box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2600
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text box labeled <guilabel>Filter:</guilabel> shows we are only looking "
"at &kword; files. By clicking on the combo box, you can select from several "
"different file formats. You can also select <guilabel>All Supported Files</"
"guilabel> to display all files that are supported by &kword;. The file types "
"available will change depending on the specific task at hand."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2606
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a mark in the checkbox labeled <guilabel>Automatically select "
"filename extension</guilabel>, then &kword; will add the correct filename "
"extension based on your selection in the <guilabel>Filter:</guilabel> drop "
"down box. If there is no mark in this box, you are responsible for providing "
"an extension. Most users will leave this box marked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> button, if you click this button, "
"the action will be aborted, and you will return to editing the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2615
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is an <guibutton>OK</guibutton> button, which will be used when we "
"have selected the correct filename."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this dialog, you can move through the folder tree to find any location "
"on your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2621
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enter a folder click on that folder. To exit that folder, click the blue "
"up arrow button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: mbtb.docbook:2624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog box is used in many different tasks in &kword;. The task will "
"determine the exact effect of the information you have entered into this "
"dialog box. For more information on the exact effect, see the documentation "
"on that task."
msgstr ""

